<title>UK: RTZ unit may take stake in aluminium venture.</title>
<headline>RTZ unit may take stake in aluminium venture.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comalco Limited, a 67 percent-owned subsidiary of RTZ-CRA Plc, said on Wednesday it may acquire up to a 50 percent equity share in Noranda Inc's Alumysa project, pending a feasibility study.</p>
<p>The Alumysa project is a potential integrated hydro-electric aluminium reduction plant complex in southern Chile.</p>
<p>In 1992 Noranda acquired water rights sufficient to supply a 270,000 tonne reduction plant, but since that time there has been over-capacity in the aluminium industry, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
